[... Other parts of policy not included ...]

Free Expression

* You have the same right to free expression on the computer system as
  you do with any other university media to which you might have
  access. This right is limited only by applicablee university, state
  and federal rules and laws (e.g. no libel, no violation of
  copyright, etc).

* Except for some narrow legal limits, you have a constitutional right
  to distribute graphically violent or pornographic material in public
  forums (see _Papish v.  University of Missouri_ for a case involving
  indecent language). The department requests, but does not demand,
