	I run a Usenet<->Fidonet gateway for an educational Fidonet
network in the state of Vermont.  It's geared primarily to educators and
teachers as well as students in the K-12 cirriculum.  I *am* in a
considerable position of responsibility but I certainly don't feel any
need to go on the Usenet-Altering-Crusade(tm) you've been trying to push.

	You say that your problem stems from the fact that Zeleny posted
to multiple groups.  Bullshit.  Your problem is that you don't have
sufficient control to keep it from happening again.  Guess what?  With the
current state of Usenet, there *ABSOLUTELY NO WAY YOU CAN PREVENT IT FROM
HAPPENING AGAIN*.  Once you come to that conclusion and *ACCEPT* it, then
and only then can you go about *DEALING* with the problem.

	And so you don't think that I'm just joining the
Gunboat-of-Flames, here are solutions I have used on our bulletin board
system that have worked:

 1) A disclaimer, that big as day that explains what you already know: That
there are some things that one will encounter on Usenet that you have no
control over.  Things such a "profanity", "offensive subject content",
"non-appropiate content subject matter", "etc.".  

 2) Limit the newsgroups your particular site gets if you're an admin. 
There is nothing that says you must carry *all* Usenet newsgroups.  In our
gateway, we only carry the k12.* and a few computer conferences.  That's
all we need.  While I may enjoy reading alt.tasteless and alt.peeves on
another unix machine, that's not the purpose of the BBS I run.  If your
university is anything like the one I attend, it can find and spend money
like water.  Surely it could find some sort of box for your department or
heck, YOU, and you can run it to your heart's content, exerting as much
control as you feel you should try to have.

 Finally, you could...

 3) DON'T USE THE USENET IN YOUR COURSE.  If you can't deal with the
problems you'll face by using Usenet (problems which I personally feel can
be easily dealt with by educating the students with an overview of Usenet;
the DO's, the DONT'Ts, the things they should EXPECT, etc.) don't use it. 
Have 'em buy another $50 book and keep 'em joyously ignorant of the world
around them.

 TTYL
 Chris
